# Testing

- `pytest` + `pytest-asyncio` + `httpx` AsyncClient
- Pure unit tests for deterministic services (no DB, no async, no mocks)
- API tests use header-based auth (`X-Dev-User-Id`) — not dependency overrides
- Multi-tenancy isolation tests for every endpoint (org2 can't see org1's data)
- Factory helpers in `tests/factories.py`
- Never call real LLM API in tests — mock it
- All tests under 5 seconds total

```python
# ❌ BAD — overriding global dependency
app.dependency_overrides[get_current_user] = lambda: user

# ✅ GOOD — header-based auth, supports multiple test clients
client = AsyncClient(headers={"X-Dev-User-Id": str(user.id)})
```
